-leaning states in the country, and Senator Jim Risch enters the final weeks as a heavy favorite over independent Todd Achilles. Risch holds the advantages of incumbency, a cash-on-hand lead of roughly $2.5 million, and a state partisan lean of about 18 points toward Republicans. Every major race rating calls the seat safe or solid for Republicans, and prediction markets give Achilles almost no chance of winning.\n\nPolling in the race has been inconsistent, with one September survey showing Achilles ahead but most other polls, including the most recent likely-voter surveys, showing Risch leading by double digits. The Iran war and cost-of-living issues have given the challenger material, and his fundraising has been respectable for an independent in Idaho, but neither has changed the race's underlying partisan structure. Achilles' pledge not to caucus with either party adds some uncertainty but does not alter the basic math.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -10.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0421, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0262, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0261, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0381, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.01, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0098, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1557, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0175, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0222, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0056, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0107, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0089, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.009, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0086, "margin": -16.0}, {"date